            <ArticleTitle>Clinical diagnosis of cavernous sinus syndromes.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>929-53</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A general approach to the complex topic of cavernous sinus syndromes is developed that attempts to make the best use of information available from the history and physical evaluation. Emphasis is on the observations and decisions that occur in the physician's office.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
